<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 92,665 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 92,665 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 92,665 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 77,136 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 4,892	    5,634</p>
<p>    Import cargo			87,773	   17,936</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours six ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Feul oil		 26,000	 Zanjan		24/9</p>
<p>Crude oil		61,000	 Capitan Mirinda   21/9</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Keefan		21/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 13,000	 Bunga Angarik     23/9</p>
<p>Motor gasoline	 26,200	 Iter		  22/9</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Santa Lucia	 31/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Strength	    21/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
